---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { RESULTS_ROWS, LIMITATIONS, REPO } from "../../data/content";
---
<Base title="Results" current="Results · unpopulated">
  <div class="eyebrow">05 · Results</div>
  <h1 class="page-title">Test-set comparison</h1>
  <p class="page-sub">
    The notebook doesn't ship with pre-executed outputs, so no numbers are fabricated here — run it end-to-end
    in Colab or locally to populate this table on your own machine. All five models are scored identically on
    NASA's official, held-out FD001 test engines.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap panel">
    <table class="results-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Model</th>
          <th>Test MAE (cycles)</th>
          <th>Test RMSE</th>
          <th>Test R²</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {RESULTS_ROWS.map((r) => (
          <tr>
            <td class="mono model-cell">{r.model}</td>
            <td class="unset">{r.mae}</td>
            <td class="unset">{r.rmse}</td>
            <td class="unset">{r.r2}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="metric-defs panel">
    <div class="metric-def">
      <span class="mono metric-name">MAE</span>
      <p>Mean Absolute Error — average absolute difference between predicted and true RUL, in cycles. The most directly interpretable metric here.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-def">
      <span class="mono metric-name">RMSE</span>
      <p>Root Mean Squared Error — like MAE but penalizes large errors more heavily.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-def">
      <span class="mono metric-name">R²</span>
      <p>Coefficient of determination — how much of the variance in true RUL is explained by the model's predictions.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="questions">
    Two questions worth checking once you have results: does any PyTorch model actually beat the Random
    Forest benchmark? And do the recurrent models (LSTM/GRU) outperform the simpler MLP/CNN — i.e. does
    explicit sequence order help on this particular fault mode?
  </p>

  <h2 class="sub-h" id="limitations">Limitations & possible extensions</h2>
  <ul class="limitations-list">
    {LIMITATIONS.map((l) => <li>{l}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <div class="reproduce panel">
    <h3>Reproduce this table</h3>
    <pre class="code-block mono">git clone {REPO.url}.git
cd {REPO.name}
jupyter notebook NASA_pytorch.ipynb</pre>
    <p>Or open it directly in <a href={REPO.colabUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Colab</a> — no manual dataset download required, the first two cells fetch and extract C-MAPSS FD001 automatically. A CUDA GPU is optional; device selection is automatic.</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-title { font-size: clamp(24px, 3vw, 32px); margin: 10px 0 12px; }
  .page-sub { color: var(--text-dim); max-width: 70ch; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 24px; }

  .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .results-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13.5px; }
  .results-table th {
    text-align: left; padding: 12px 20px; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--text-faint); text-transform: uppercase; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-hair);
  }
  .results-table td { padding: 12px 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-hair); }
  .results-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  .model-cell { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .unset { color: var(--text-faint); font-style: italic; font-size: 12.5px; }

  .metric-defs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 0; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .metric-def { padding: 18px 20px; border-right: 1px solid var(--line-hair); }
  .metric-def:last-child { border-right: none; }
  .metric-name { color: var(--telemetry-cyan); font-size: 13px; }
  .metric-def p { margin: 8px 0 0; color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.6; }

  .questions { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.7; max-width: 70ch; margin: 0 0 8px; }

  .sub-h { font-size: 19px; margin: 40px 0 14px; }
  .limitations-list { padding-left: 20px; margin: 0 0 30px; color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.9; max-width: 74ch; }
  .limitations-list li { margin-bottom: 6px; }

  .reproduce { padding: 22px 24px; }
  .reproduce h3 { font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .reproduce .code-block { margin-bottom: 12px; color: var(--telemetry-cyan); }
  .reproduce p { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 13px; margin: 0; }
  .reproduce a { color: var(--telemetry-cyan); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .metric-defs { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .metric-def { border-right: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-hair); }
    .metric-def:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  }
</style>
